<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 29.9 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in March 1997 versus 30.5 million lbs in February and 36.7 million lbs in March 1996 the Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1997 period amounted to 86.9 million lbs versus 102.6 million lbs in the 1996 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
</text>
